<Layout title="About FileNest — Our approach and roadmap">
  <article class="prose-page wrap"><div class="eyebrow">A LITTLE LESS FRICTION</div><h1>Useful tools.<br />Room to breathe.</h1><p>FileNest is a growing collection of small tools for your everyday files. The idea is simple: get from the file you have to the file you need, without creating an account or uploading its contents to a conversion server.</p><h2>Available in this first release</h2><ul><li>Markdown preview and standalone HTML export.</li><li>Markdown PDF export through your browser’s print dialog.</li><li>Text comparison with optional case and whitespace rules.</li><li>Structural JSON comparison that ignores object-key order.</li><li>CSV to JSON and JSON to CSV conversion.</li></ul><h2>Next on the workbench</h2><p>Image resize, compression, and format conversion; images to PDF; PDF merge, split, and page organisation. These are planned features, not available tools yet.</p><h2>Built around local processing</h2><p>Our current tools run on your device. Inputs disappear when you leave or reload the page. We do not store a copy, so download results you need to keep. Device memory and browser support limit the size of jobs we can process.</p><h2>How we will support the project</h2><p>This first release is free and has no advertising or paid features. Advertising and optional paid workflows may support future development. We will update our privacy information before introducing external analytics, advertising, or server-based processing.</p></article>
</Layout>
